  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 103.11 Forest management activities",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 103.11 “Forest management activities” means activities necessary for forest management as defined in RSA 227-G:2, IX, including but not limited to extracting timber, planting and replanting of various species, and cutting roads and pathways through forests, provided such activities are undertaken in compliance with applicable statutes and rules, including RSA 227-J, and best management practices.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19",
